WEBVTT

00:00.210 --> 00:01.680
Instructor: All right, so in this section,

00:01.680 --> 00:03.750
we're focusing on Git tags,

00:03.750 --> 00:06.210
which we have not really talked about at all,

00:06.210 --> 00:08.880
but they're pretty straightforward, nothing super difficult,

00:08.880 --> 00:12.240
and they're also not used all the time.

00:12.240 --> 00:15.360
It depends on the project, it depends on the company,

00:15.360 --> 00:17.850
or the organization that you're working with,

00:17.850 --> 00:20.100
or just your personal habits.

00:20.100 --> 00:21.660
Most often these days,

00:21.660 --> 00:24.510
tags are used to mark different releases,

00:24.510 --> 00:27.900
different versions of a project over time,

00:27.900 --> 00:32.900
like, you know, version 7.1.0, version 7.1.1, and so on.

00:33.450 --> 00:35.130
So important to understand.

00:35.130 --> 00:38.070
I'll say understanding Git tags is important.

00:38.070 --> 00:42.840
Understanding semantic versioning is not really tied to Git.

00:42.840 --> 00:45.060
This is a concept on its own.

00:45.060 --> 00:47.700
I'm teetering between important and nice to have,

00:47.700 --> 00:50.490
'cause it is, it's kind of these days

00:50.490 --> 00:53.310
like the de facto use case for tags.

00:53.310 --> 00:56.130
But anyway, I'm getting ahead of myself.

00:56.130 --> 00:58.860
I'll say that viewing tags is important.

00:58.860 --> 01:02.190
Creating tags, lightweight and annotated tags, is important,

01:02.190 --> 01:04.920
and being able to push tags is important.

01:04.920 --> 01:08.850
Moving tags, diffing tags, deleting tags, nice to have.

01:08.850 --> 01:11.280
I mean, it's all kind of in this gray area

01:11.280 --> 01:13.050
between important and nice to have,

01:13.050 --> 01:15.840
but nothing in my opinion that is critical here.

01:15.840 --> 01:17.910
If you end up working with tags a lot,

01:17.910 --> 01:19.200
you'll get very good with them,

01:19.200 --> 01:21.090
and it's very straightforward.

01:21.090 --> 01:23.370
Honestly, they're pretty simple.

01:23.370 --> 01:26.370
So I think it's worth checking out the section.

01:26.370 --> 01:28.020
For as many videos as there are,

01:28.020 --> 01:29.730
it's actually pretty short.

01:29.730 --> 01:33.480
Some of them are like one minute, or one and a half minutes,

01:33.480 --> 01:35.520
so don't let it intimidate you

01:35.520 --> 01:37.860
that there's 11 videos, or something.

01:37.860 --> 01:39.060
Anyway, let's get started.

01:39.060 --> 01:41.253
We're gonna talk about tags, here we go.
